## Data Model Requirements

This feature uses the existing `mileage_logs` and `service_logs` tables. It must not create duplicate mileage or service tables.

### `mileage_logs` table

| Field | Type | Rules |
|-------|------|-------|
| `mileage_log_id` | INTEGER | Primary key |
| `vehicle_id` | INTEGER | Foreign key referencing `vehicles.vehicle_id`; NOT NULL |
| `date_recorded` | DATE | NOT NULL |
| `current_mileage` | INTEGER | NOT NULL; must be non-negative |

### `service_logs` table

| Field | Type | Rules |
|-------|------|-------|
| `service_log_id` | INTEGER | Primary key |
| `vehicle_id` | INTEGER | Foreign key referencing `vehicles.vehicle_id`; NOT NULL |
| `service_date` | DATE | NOT NULL |
| `service_performed` | TEXT | NOT NULL |

The existing `vehicles` table remains part of the shared data model.

### Associations

- A vehicle can have multiple mileage records.
- Each mileage record belongs to one vehicle.
- A vehicle can have multiple service records.
- Each service record belongs to one vehicle.
- Mileage and service records must be accessible according to the area associated with their vehicle.

